+/* PCONTEXT: VEH register state.
+ *
+ * This used to be an opaque void* on Linux "since Linux callers don't use
+ * it". They do: the NV2A MMIO hook decodes the faulting instruction out of
+ * Rip and reads/writes the general registers, which is the only way a title
